## Sequence Analysis

Sequence analysis is a fundamental step in bioinformatics that helps identify similarities, conserved regions, and evolutionary
relationships among biological sequences. It provides valuable insights into the structure, function, and evolutionary history of genes
and proteins, making it an essential component of biological research.

In this project, sequence analysis was carried out using a combination of bioinformatics tools. The analysis began with BLAST 
(Basic Local Alignment Search Tool), which was used to compare the query protein sequence against biological databases to identify 
homologous sequences with significant similarity. The retrieved sequences were then subjected to Multiple Sequence Alignment (MSA)
using Clustal Omega, allowing the identification of conserved amino acid residues and regions shared among different species. Finally, 
phylogenetic analysis was performed using the aligned sequences to infer evolutionary relationships and construct a phylogenetic tree, 
providing a graphical representation of the evolutionary divergence and relatedness of the selected protein sequences.

